  "behavior": [
    "Typed coherent presentation and management reads share one real backing transaction. Authenticated journals are reused only inside that synchronous read, keyed by service/Space/through. Context is removed on every return or failure; no authority is cached across transactions/accounts/nodes/processes.",
    "Native publish/select consume the coherent snapshot while preserving draft versions, pixel anchors, channel scope and the existing fresh durable-management overlay under its lock. Urgent delivery still avoids rebuilding the readable timeline.",
    "Real SQLite fault-trigger installation/removal shares the same canonical-file application gate, with off-main checks. The gate is released before UI actions and cleanup retains original failures. This replaces another connection busy handler without changing product transaction locks or native deadlines."
  ],
  "motivation": "Actual sourcecf publication span92138\u201393759ms held1621 overlaps940ms ofa1052ms create-lock wait; earlier3112ms holder not proven. Batching removes repeated authentication and transaction setup. No measured native improvement claimed yet. Earlier actual SQLITE_BUSY setup remains retained; source maintenance coordination still needs actual runtime proof.",
